Yippee! After a month examing, it's back to nethack, and two ascensions
in quick succession. Caveman, and tourist, to add to the healer.
Spoilers and comments follow.



It was my first time on the caveman quest. Neat touch with the closed
entry-way. Went all the way back to the gnomish mines for a pickaxe, 
then found wall too hard anyway!
Chomatic dragon beaten with handy wando'death found in shop on level 2.
Lots of shops in the game. Loads of magic lamps in minetown. Equipped
early on, once holy water factory established, and never looked back.

Weapons: Excalibur - my first real use of it. Hmm. OK, I guess, but nowhere
near as flash as my beloved magicbane. (I hate curses). On principle, I
don't use helms of opp alignment. (Bad roleplaying to do it consciously, I
feel). I didn't know it gave level-drain protection, though. I never
really seem to suffer from that prob anyway.

I played cautiously, as ever. Plan: use shops to identify id scrolls, then
whip up loads of holy water, bless id scrolls and I'm away. Normally end up
completing quest before iding much.

Tourist ascension was much more fun. I like tourists - I just tend to
be accident prone with them (Embarrassing scenes with falling drawbridges
et al). Took *no* chances once I had my hands on the wandowishing (only 2 
charges! sob! hooray for PYEC). Genocided ;,L,cockatrices,P,V (in that order).

Incidentally, I noticed my gauntlets of power (old gloves) could rust. It
seems this is always true, whatever their external description.

Best break: found AoR in gnomish mines. Definitely saved my life on the quest
when, thanks to a poly trap, I was unexpectedly confronted by a black dragon,
which hit me with its blast before I had a chance to move. Later found an
aleax with SoR for more traditional tactics.

Worst Break: The Lady gave me *DragonBane* (groan). And nothing else. When
I created my first batch of holy water (14 thereof...), I was prompty made
Envoy of Balance. Quite handy, but I never got anything else out of her.
So Vorpal Blade (eventually +4) was my constant companion. Nice beheading
trick, but I missed magic bane, especially at the end with curses flying thick
and fast.

I think tourists are actually quite a powerful class. You just have to be
careful, and not gain too much experience before knocking off a hobbit for its
elven chain. With the PYEC, the world's your oyster.

Wizard kept bothering me (9 times) but no double trouble - interestingly,
my healer never encountered that either, so it was a real shock when it
happened to me the first time. Wandodeath+PYEC=no worries. He only got his
grubby paws on the amulet once - on the plane of fire.

My best career move was using a wish for a blessed spellbook of magic mapping.
With one re-write, that enabled me to completely map gehennon, and saved
*so much time*.

  Julyan.


